i'll be honest with you guys new pokemon  snap can be really cryptic sometimes  i found myself stuck and not knowing how  to progress numerous times but after  beating the game i noticed there were  specific things that usually advance  the story even if the game doesn't tell  you so in an effort to help my fellow  photographers i wanted to break down  things you can try if you find yourself  stuck  in new pokemon snap if you like this  video then consider dropping a like and  subscribing  we'd appreciate it so first things first  let's talk about research levels  when you complete a course your photos  will be evaluated by professor mir and  you'll get a score on those photos  that score becomes expedition points and  you'll need a certain amount of  expedition points to unlock the next  research level in any given course  a new research level means more pokemon  and potential new behaviors for the  pokemon that were already there  what the game doesn't tell you is that a  lot of the time you need to get to  research level 2 to advance the story  and at least for me i didn't always get  to research level 2 my first time around  so i needed to go through the course  again to get more expedition points  as a little bonus tip to that you should  still snap pokemon you've already  snapped when going through a course  again  and having the professor evaluate them  for expedition points even though it  won't increase your photo decks it'll  help you get to the next research level  faster  you never need to get past level 2 on  any of the courses if you're just trying  to beat the main story  but i do want to point out that at one  point in the game you get the option to  take photos around the lab and you do  not need to get the level 2 on that one  the expedition points required for that  one is a lot larger than the regular  courses and it has no bearing on the  story so don't be like me  and play that course a dozen times only  for nothing to happen before i move on i  want to briefly mention that you'll  reach a point where you start getting  requests from your team members  and while they're a great way to get  some four-star photos they have nothing  to do with story progression so if  you're stuck  don't start trying to do a bunch of  requests like i also did so okay  you have every main course up to  research level two and you still haven't  progressed  now what can you do well try lumen orbs  to unlock some lumen orbs you'll need to  take a photo of the glowing crystal  bloom on each island  yes there's a different colored lumina  orb for each island that only works on  that island  you must take a photo of a glowing  crystal bloom once that aren't glowing  don't count  and then once you do that the professor  will be able to make the new lumina orbs  for that island  sometimes that'll be enough to progress  but if that doesn't work  try going through the course again and  actually using the illumina orbs  sometimes the professor just wants to  see it in action and i respect that  this next part is going to get a little  more specific to later parts of the game  so if you haven't gotten through the  forest lumina spot yet i'd recommend  getting to that point with the  information i've already given and then  coming back  alright so you've gotten to that point  in the game great this is where things  get  super cryptic after you've taken photos  of the second luminous pokemon you'll  learn that there are more luminous  pokemon  two more to be specific but how do you  get to them the game tells you nothing  so here's what you have to do to get the  first one you'll need to play research  level 2 of the volcano because it leads  down a completely separate path  not an alternate path it just is a  separate path  how would you know to do this you  wouldn't so hopefully you just felt like  playing the volcano level again  but once you start volcano level 2 it's  pretty straightforward the other one is  probably the most frustrating and also  probably why a lot of you are here  in c4 level two you'll notice that claw  its are at the beginning of the level  it'll start swimming in front of you and  you'll notice it try to destroy some  rocks in a cave but it isn't strong  enough to do it  what you're supposed to do is hit this  pokemon with a lumina orb and that  powers it up so it'll destroy the rocks  and open a new path to you  you'll need to take a photo of the  glowing crystal bloom in the sea floor  and unlock the lumina ore before  attempting this  this gameplay mechanic was never used  before and is never used again  so if you didn't know to do that i do  not blame you at all from there just  follow the new path and you'll be on  your way to the fourth lumen of pokemon  moving on once you reach the cave on the  fifth island it's actually similar to  the third lumen of pokemon in the  volcano  just play through research level 2  normally after you unlock it and it'll  lead down a new path  now beyond this is endgame spoilers so  if you haven't unlocked the sixth and  final island  come back once you do in the final area  ruins of remembrance  you first want to get the glowing  crystal bloom which is actually very  close to the beginning of the course  once you do that and professor mira  creates this island's lumen orb  go through the course again and this  time light up all the flowers in the  cave itself  they can be pretty tricky to spot and  make sure you hit them before the neo1  gets too far away or you'll have to  start the course over once you do that a  new route will unlock and you'll be on  your way to the final lumen of pokemon  and there you have it hopefully this  helped you progress through some of the  more cryptic parts of new pokemon snap  have any further questions drop them  down in the comments below and i'll try  to answer them as best as i can  if you're curious to see the differences  between pokemon snap and new pokemon  snap i made another video listing off  six of the biggest changes between the  two  thanks for watching and for all things  pokemon stay tuned to gamespot  [Music]  you
 

